{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite","id":923441,"title":"Vigilant Times: Take 2! [Open Invite]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-29T13:17:40-07:00","id":923441,"title":"Vigilant Times: Take 2! [Open Invite]","content":"long time ago, I've started a brainstorming thread in the subject of &quot;Ancient Bloodlines&quot; like fan-book- which had a lot of good ideas but a lot of it wasn't really developed. Lately, I have started to ponder again in the subject, and I've thought to myself why not to try again? Anyway, I've decided that this time I'll take a more practical approach and suggest one Era per time unit (a week maybe? I have tests you know), and see what I can think about hunters during that Era and hear what other people has to say about it (I think we should go chronically, something possible mostly thanks to Second Chance's hard work about CofD's timeline), and while most of the focus should be about existing/future/unchosen Eras and similar historical setting books, if someone feels inspired for a new timeline or something feel free to suggest it (I should have a complete list of fan suggested Eras somewhere. I'll check if someone is interested)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gVwCuWzpYdccPgMiR4k_2FStWelNNfIDVHA1LXk-gXw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">full list of ideas per Era</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, let's start from, well the start- Sundered World.<br /> <br /> Like everyone know, that Era has a Mage-Werewolf focus, although there have been more than few suggestions for other gamelines. It has, after all, one of the richer Crossover sidebars, which includes a lot of potential- from primordial vampires and chthonic Bound and up to alchemist potters and the Shaniatu far in the south. Hunters are also mentioned in the sidebar, but only as a passing reference, as one of the possible people who stand against ravaging beasts. Now, in many ways, Sundered World is the darkest Dark Era in the book- there are very few points of light, when the very theme of the book is &quot;do as the Wise say, or you are dead&quot;. In a way, that should put the hunters in the shadow of the Wise- they are the protectors of their community, after all. They are the ones who know what the community needs to do if it wish to survive. Death is at every corner, and only the Wise can protect the People. There is not other way.<br /> <br /> But there is. Challenging the status que of the overreaching darkness is part of their theme. This may be humanity's darkest time, but it also should be the time when those lone candles shine the brightest. In this time, when people has to follow thousands of taboos and obey their gods and Wise without second guest, those who dare to rise against the order and act on their own for what they think as &quot;right&quot;, those who dare to leave the warm embrace of the fire and search the wilderness for new wonders and threats, the ones who risk their very life by acting outside their community in order to protect their community are the hunters of the Era- few points in the darkness, but they shine more brightly than any other.<br /> <br /> Such lifestyle means that most potential hunter should either be traders or, well, hunters- although the fact that any person could take on the Vigil is one of the game's themes (well, other than the Wise). The Era itself should also put a lot of emphasis around 1st Tier game- most of those early hunters would end up as cultural heroes, people who with of without help of the Wise and the gods defeated the many terrors of the ancient world. Those hunters you play in that Era may end up as the origin for stories like Hercules, Gilgamesh, Durga... and Marduk.<br /> <br /> So, just from the top of my head, here are some ideas for potential &quot;hunter types&quot;- the most common ones should be, like I've said before, the hunters. Those people know the wilderness the best, and they also know how to track down and hunt different monsters. They cult-like structure allows them to preserve many traditions and stories, allowing them to maintain a certain amount of information about the different demons and gods of the time. Traders should also have a certain amount of information, and in that time knowing in which paths one should walk and in which he should not in critical if you wish to survive. Other than that, you also have the regular Joe kind of hunters who have just stumbled upon a monster and actually killed it, like the kind of people described in the sidebar who are simply strong willed enough to recognize a Beast and kill it (although pre-modern Heroes may be indistinguishable from them, and who knows how should they operate in that time). Finally, the last &quot;hunter option&quot; which I can think about are some sort of guardians to the Wise- mortal men and women who serve them as hands and legs and swear to give their life in order to protect them. Ironically, those &quot;cancer cells&quot; would be the most accepted hunters in that Era.<br /> <br /> Now, while I've said that it should be a 1st Tier Era, let's try to muse about some higher Tiers, and if we already do so than let's go all extreme and think about something which is, practically, unthinkable- a conspiracy. Now, I know that an organization in the standards of modern conspiracy is unthinkable, but I also believe that Tiers should be a subjective terms- when all of your world revolves around the River, the Forest, the Mountain and the Sea, a &quot;3rd Tier organization&quot; should simply be a group which is able to operate through the many small Vinca communities, and I already thought about a candidate- the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/634487-the-nibiru-conspiracy\">Nibiru </a>(or, as they call themselves, as the Wolf-Hunter Cult), which I've also included a sidebar for them about that Era. That group was developed as being the &quot;first&quot;, and the thought was making them show up in the Neolithic. As someone has noticed, their Endowments are similar in many ways with what Heroes do, which should work as the hero-hunter mix of the time. As you could imagine, they would work inside the hunter-cults of the time, worshiping Father Wolf and the Nine Firstborn who gave them their blessings- plus, they could be awesome to use as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dacians#Mythological_theories\" target=\"_blank\">wolf masked dancers</a> of that culture. Finally, the fact they target both spirits and witches makes them as a good foe in that Era, with a good reason for attacking and objecting the Wise, unlike most of the other People (they go through the wilderness and find the dead corpses of the gods, understanding who is the one responsible to the acts), turning them into permanent outsiders and a good foil for any &quot;temple guardian&quot; who side with the Wise.<br /> <br /> So- what kind of ideas/suggestions do you have for that dark, dark Era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 11-12-2018, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T16:06:33-07:00","id":924663,"title":"","content":"I haven't really thought them out or anything but just offhand.<br /> <br /> For one thing, you would have the Knights of St. George. They would go under another name obviously, but from Witch Finders p101, 'Dragonslayers stood apart from human settlements before the time of Ur, the first city of Sumer and the dawn of human civilization. Their lot was the death of witches, and nothing more.'<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I feel there should be an 'undead' focused group. People who have become outcast due to their association with the dead. Someone who fed their vampiric relative, becoming weak and addicted to the point that they were ostracized by their village. By the time the vampire moved on they had nothing left. Or those who have been haunted or attacked by ghosts and bear their marks, ashen handprints stained onto their skin and white streaks through otherwise youthful hair. I figure they would be picked up by others who had organized and devoted the rest of their lives to ridding the world of the monsters that made them what they are. I like the idea of calling them the Stricken or Silent, perhaps in a link to Sin-Eaters, but also because Stricken could fit to how their 'sorry lot' began. Silent could be a defense they use, as talking to ghosts can give them something to cling to, especially for their anchors.<br /> <br /> And lastly, I'd need to check out the Slashers book but if I recall correctly there was a theory that Nimrod was one of the first, and the idea of these other primeval legends as a sort of naturally created icon or defense mechanism against the dangerous shadows of the world. I could see them as members of the first true hunter cells, humans at the top of the aggression scale who focus it outward. If you wanted you could tie it into the Heroes of Beast, without the Beast part. Beast the Primordial core book p201, 'In the past, this sort of person would never experience the Devouring, but rather served a different purpose. A Hero could act as an early warning, sensing that the monsters were coming and giving people time to learn their lessons on their own, without fear or pain.' Heroes weren't focused on the Beast-killing at that point and mostly kept to defending and helping humanity. Though I could see them as individual members of compacts and cells, rather than groups of them acting together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T01:22:20-07:00","id":924815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=924663#post924663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't really thought them out or anything but just offhand.<br /> <br /> For one thing, you would have the Knights of St. George. They would go under another name obviously, but from Witch Finders p101, 'Dragonslayers stood apart from human settlements before the time of Ur, the first city of Sumer and the dawn of human civilization. Their lot was the death of witches, and nothing more.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch! The fact they &quot;stood apart&quot; makes sense considering the role of the Wise in that Era. Unfortunately, it seems like the Vinca didn't had anything &quot;dragon-like&quot; in their culture (at least, not from what I can gather), and there was definitely nothing like the Faceless Angels, not to mention that the Knights' mythology i way too complicated to that time. I've personally always leaned toward the &quot;Abyssal Interpretation&quot; for the Knights, so perhaps we could tie them to the Outside, and maybe we could even use the shards of the Time Before as part of that (maybe they are the descendants of a small community who tried to live in such a shard and drew the attention of something which shouldn't be exist, or maybe their Wise was corrupted by the Outside and had to be killed, something which required making a pact of their own with the Void.<br /> <br /> That would also make me think about the Aegis Kai Doru. While it seems natural to make them as witch/shifter hunters, during that Era the Sundering didn't yet happened, and as we all know Atlantis never happened. In that case, what if the events told by the Guardians are truly separate events, and that during that Era they still don't see witches and werewolves as enemies? I think that they could work well during that Era as the &quot;temple guardians of the Wise&quot; in one form or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Otherwise, I feel there should be an 'undead' focused group. People who have become outcast due to their association with the dead. Someone who fed their vampiric relative, becoming weak and addicted to the point that they were ostracized by their village. By the time the vampire moved on they had nothing left. Or those who have been haunted or attacked by ghosts and bear their marks, ashen handprints stained onto their skin and white streaks through otherwise youthful hair. I figure they would be picked up by others who had organized and devoted the rest of their lives to ridding the world of the monsters that made them what they are. I like the idea of calling them the Stricken or Silent, perhaps in a link to Sin-Eaters, but also because Stricken could fit to how their 'sorry lot' began. Silent could be a defense they use, as talking to ghosts can give them something to cling to, especially for their anchors. </div> </div> </div>well, the dead are one of the biggest concerns to the People. Maybe I could tie them somehow to either the Cainte Heresy or the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/38053-dying-conspiracy-ebony-fangs\">Ebony Fangs</a> (which, if the later, would be before the foundation of Kigal- or maybe the foundations for that myth would start in that Era).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And lastly, I'd need to check out the Slashers book but if I recall correctly there was a theory that Nimrod was one of the first, and the idea of these other primeval legends as a sort of naturally created icon or defense mechanism against the dangerous shadows of the world. I could see them as members of the first true hunter cells, humans at the top of the aggression scale who focus it outward. If you wanted you could tie it into the Heroes of Beast, without the Beast part. Beast the Primordial core book p201, 'In the past, this sort of person would never experience the Devouring, but rather served a different purpose. A Hero could act as an early warning, sensing that the monsters were coming and giving people time to learn their lessons on their own, without fear or pain.' Heroes weren't focused on the Beast-killing at that point and mostly kept to defending and helping humanity. Though I could see them as individual members of compacts and cells, rather than groups of them acting together. </div> </div> </div>I personally think that neolithic Heroes better represent individuals like Nimrod because, well, he really feels as psycho. Still, it is too early for Nimrod himself I think, and the wrong geographic region, but I do like that Neolithic Hero Interpretation. Also- we should think about Neolithic Slashers, simply because that sounds really scary :P<br /> <br /> Another food for thought- Thule's Rmoahalas. They should be around, shouldn't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T07:41:03-07:00","id":924879,"title":"","content":"I think the Sundering fits pretty well with the modern AKD beliefs. I mean, the Wise of the Vinca were already attacking Pangeans and stealing their hearts whilst maintaining the lie to the sleepers that they were a freely given gift. Their intentions were good(ish), but killing Gods and covering it up is a pretty paradigmatic example of hubris.<br /> <br /> When the Sundering happens (whether the Wise are involved or not*) it's not a great leap for some sleeper temple guards to come to the conclusion that the Wise are to blame for destroying Pangea and sundering the world.<br /> <br /> *On the one hand, it's the Uratha's story and we don't necessarily want the Awakened dominating the story, but on the otherhand it is an interesting coincidence that the Wise were already attacking Pangeans when the greatest of the Pangeans is killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T08:37:08-07:00","id":924888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite#post923441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, the last &quot;hunter option&quot; which I can think about are some sort of guardians to the Wise- mortal men and women who serve them as hands and legs and swear to give their life in order to protect them. Ironically, those &quot;cancer cells&quot; would be the most accepted hunters in that Era.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=924815#post924815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would also make me think about the Aegis Kai Doru. While it seems natural to make them as witch/shifter hunters, during that Era the Sundering didn't yet happened, and as we all know Atlantis never happened. In that case, what if the events told by the Guardians are truly separate events, and that during that Era they still don't see witches and werewolves as enemies? I think that they could work well during that Era as the &quot;temple guardians of the Wise&quot; in one form or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see something like the Guardian-Summoner dynamic from Final Fantasy X working for such hunters. Not only that, but they would probably all be Sleepwalkers (or &quot;ember bearers&quot;, to them), which would allow them to protect the Wise even as they are working their magic. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=924879#post924879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Sundering fits pretty well with the modern AKD beliefs. I mean, the Wise of the Vinca were already attacking Pangeans and stealing their hearts whilst maintaining the lie to the sleepers that they were a freely given gift. Their intentions were good(ish), but killing Gods and covering it up is a pretty paradigmatic example of hubris.<br /> <br /> When the Sundering happens (whether the Wise are involved or not*) it's not a great leap for some sleeper temple guards to come to the conclusion that the Wise are to blame for destroying Pangea and sundering the world.<br /> <br /> *On the one hand, it's the Uratha's story and we don't necessarily want the Awakened dominating the story, but on the otherhand it is an interesting coincidence that the Wise were already attacking Pangeans when the greatest of the Pangeans is killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, seeing as the Aegis (in 1E) had a big grudge against Mages <i>and</i> Werewolves, I can second that. Granted, the conspiracy as we know it likely came together around the time of To the Strongest. But I'm having an easier time, now, picturing their founding members as the inheritors of an ancient myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T12:38:34-07:00","id":924988,"title":"","content":"If we are working on the Aegis, we should also think how to represent the &quot;stolen/lost power&quot; they had as artificers and enchanters. It should be something a bit bigger than the Relic Maker merit- you know, something that cloud actually be lost once the relationships between the Wise and the Guardians goes wary after the Sundering. Maybe the Wise could have transplanted a part of their soul (or even an Omphalos Stone) in the Guardians in order to allow them make certain imbued items?<br /> <br /> Also, another thought about the Knights of St George- considering that in the original Atlantis myth the creations of the Demesne was a gift of the dragons if I'm not mistaken, and that in Sundered World it is actually the hearts of Pangaea's gods, wouldn't it mean that in the Knights' myth than the Pangaeans should take the Dragons' place? And if the Angels are rivals to the Dragons, what would that make them? Abyssal Pangaeans of some sort?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T13:52:24-07:00","id":925026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=924988#post924988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are working on the Aegis, we should also think how to represent the &quot;stolen/lost power&quot; they had as artificers and enchanters. It should be something a bit bigger than the Relic Maker merit- you know, something that cloud actually be lost once the relationships between the Wise and the Guardians goes wary after the Sundering. Maybe the Wise could have transplanted a part of their soul (or even an Omphalos Stone) in the Guardians in order to allow them make certain imbued items?</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea would be that the distant ancestors of the AKD are the potter caste. I mean, it's stated that they hold a special status with their own special quasi-magical knowledge. They manufacture the ritual tools that the society uses; and in an era where the Guantlet isn't around and the Shadow is a very real part of life, those items have real power. When the Sundering occurs, the potters are going to be out of luck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, another thought about the Knights of St George- considering that in the original Atlantis myth the creations of the Demesne was a gift of the dragons if I'm not mistaken, and that in Sundered World it is actually the hearts of Pangaea's gods, wouldn't it mean that in the Knights' myth than the Pangaeans should take the Dragons' place? And if the Angels are rivals to the Dragons, what would that make them? Abyssal Pangaeans of some sort? </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty good idea. The Faceless Angels don't need to be elaborated on really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T01:41:31-07:00","id":925270,"title":"","content":"the AKD as potters would make tons of sense. The only thing I would like to see is bits of their mythology being &quot;real&quot;- especially the part about Asterion and the Mistress of Honey, at least partially. We all know who the former would be in the setting- but what about the Mistress? <br /> <br /> As for the Knights- if we do use the &quot;Pangaeans as dragons&quot; option, that should make the proto-Knights into people who object using the Omphalus Stones and see it as &quot;unnatural&quot;, or an act against the gods, or that they should maintain the &quot;old ways&quot;. They may be the &quot;barbarians&quot; of the time, living apart of the community without Wise of their own- and by doing so, they stumble upon secrets better stay hidden, and draw the attention of something which was kept asleep.<br /> <br /> Also, I still think that the Rmoahalas should show up in the setting- they are an interesting part Hunter's lore, and they fit to the time period. Plus, they add an interesting layer of weirdness to the setting, and could be tied either to one of the Time Before shards or just be a pre-human race who exist in that &quot;Primal Era&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T03:13:44-07:00","id":925287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=925270#post925270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The AKD as potters would make tons of sense. The only thing I would like to see is bits of their mythology being &quot;real&quot;- especially the part about Asterion and the Mistress of Honey, at least partially. We all know who the former would be in the setting- but what about the Mistress?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the Mistress is another Pangaean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=925270#post925270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Knights- if we do use the &quot;Pangaeans as dragons&quot; option, that should make the proto-Knights into people who object using the Omphalus Stones and see it as &quot;unnatural&quot;, or an act against the gods, or that they should maintain the &quot;old ways&quot;. They may be the &quot;barbarians&quot; of the time, living apart of the community without Wise of their own- and by doing so, they stumble upon secrets better stay hidden, and draw the attention of something which was kept asleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a semi-related note to this, I had this concept in my head for a while. Banishers and/or hunters in the Neolithic Era who consider it their duty to destroy the Omphalos Stones and punish the Wise for their transgressions. On a less violent note, there could also exist hunters and Wise who seek out and protect the remains of dead Pangaeans while hunting for their Omphalos Stones to facilitate their revival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T04:31:25-07:00","id":925297,"title":"","content":"I agree with Deionscribe, the Mistress of Honey makes a pretty reasonable Pangean. I mean, bees and other polinating insects are an important natural cycle. Honey has been collected by humans for a very long time.<br /> <br /> On a related note; in the optional rules for the AKD, they swear their oath on an 'Oath Stone', a small rock broken off a much larger sacred stone. As a result of this oath the AKD member can utilise the relics of witches and werewolves. Perhaps that original rock is an Omphalos stone and by undergoing the special trial and then swearing an oath over it, the AKD member can make themselves a sleepwalker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T04:48:42-07:00","id":925299,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about the Mistress as Pangaean, simply because she was described as having &quot;unliving body&quot;- something which rings more familiar with that bee like vampire bloodline. There are higher chances of her being connected to the Ocean Beyond Life as some sort of Chthonian or other Underworld monstrosity. On the other hand, the Mistress was never said to be Bee, but that her body contains bees. Her preview is honey- and apparently, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_honeyguide\" target=\"_blank\">Bird </a>may have been the one giving that secret to the People. The gifts of the Bull and the Bird bringing the end of the Primal Era works perfectly to the Neolithic.<br /> <br /> As for the Knights as punishers of the Wise- there is a small problem, I think. As far as I understand, the Wise hide the fact that they kill Pangaeans in order to get their hearts. While certain groups (like Wolf's hunters) may suspect, most of the community believe them to be gifts from the gods. I think that the proto-Knights would see the very fact that they use the Ompahlos Stones as a &quot;sin&quot;, and that the &quot;gifts of the gods&quot; are ways to corrupt the natural ways of the world. The Faceless Angels would be seen as more of a force during that time- that is, they worship the &quot;natural order of the world&quot;, with whatever the angels are being how that force regulates itself. Hunters who try to return dead Pangaeans to life using Omphalos Stones should totally be a thing (that would be one of the goals of the Nibiru during that time, I believe)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T04:51:01-07:00","id":925302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=925297#post925297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note; in the optional rules for the AKD, they swear their oath on an 'Oath Stone', a small rock broken off a much larger sacred stone. As a result of this oath the AKD member can utilise the relics of witches and werewolves. Perhaps that original rock is an Omphalos stone and by undergoing the special trial and then swearing an oath over it, the AKD member can make themselves a sleepwalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is a rule which I actually use in my games, so I'll totally be in favor for that idea :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T05:12:33-07:00","id":925303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=925299#post925299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about the Mistress as Pangaean, simply because she was described as having &quot;unliving body&quot;- something which rings more familiar with that bee like vampire bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very nice catch. Now you say that, I wonder if that's meant to be a direct reference?<br /> The thing is, when you're trying to reconcile different pieces of the setting, you're going to need to sand down bits of it to fit. Bear in mind that large elements of their mythology are already wrong. I mean, the Uratha aren't the descendants of a Honey god and a minotaur. You need to really stretch to work out how those fit with the Moon and Wolf.<br /> <br /> Another group with some potential relevance is the Promethean Brotherhood (actually, the Rite of Hecate). What happens if a village doesn't have any Wise to protect it? Maybe you go and steal somone elses wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T12:45:05-07:00","id":925468,"title":"","content":"Wise-less communities attacking others to gain wisdom of their own in a primal fight of survival? Sounds very Neolithic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> All in all, I like how the Wise-hunter dynamics is forming for this Era- the Wise are the foundation for the Vinca's society, and hunters either directly oppose them (the Knights), protect and serve them (AKD), steal them (Promethean Brotherhood) or try to offer an alternative (the Nibiru). On the other hand, we also need to remember that there are other dangers out there- Werewolves take a part equal in that Era to that of the Wise, while Beasts and the Dead are constant threats. While the Nibiru have some relatively peaceful relationships with the Uratha, the AKD would probably be more antagonistic (they may be one of the few groups who know the truth about the stolen Stones, as they guide and protect their Wise in Pangaea and the Shadow). The Les Mysteres may exist in some primitive form as shamans, but they may be indistinguishable from the Wise for most people, and they won't have that focus around Werewolf as their modern incarnation has- in fact, I believe that they would be a very different organization in that time. Also, I still think that hunters of the trader caste would be worth to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T15:06:52-07:00","id":925521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=925468#post925468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I still think that hunters of the trader caste would be worth to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason, I'm thinking of the Hototogisu as a possible reference.<br /> <br /> Another idea that comes to mind is a Neolithic take on your Museum Secretorum, since &quot;one way or another, it has always existed&quot;. I have to wonder, though, whether they are a tradition that would have originated from the Vinca. Or, like the <i>Gudthabak</i>, they hail from a different culture/people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 07-03-2016, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:36:55-07:00","id":925584,"title":"","content":"To be fair, regarding the Knights, it's likely they keep their own workings secret and it's probably not impossible for them to discover the secret murders the Wise are committing. The average mortal likely wouldn't simply because they're homebodies, while Knights are wandering warriors.<br /> <br /> And while the Tower of Babel and Nimrod are possibly after the Vinca times, in the Dark Era there's explicitly a 'Tower of Babel' like plothook involving an idigam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T00:29:58-07:00","id":925779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=925521#post925521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason, I'm thinking of the Hototogisu as a possible reference.<br /> <br /> Another idea that comes to mind is a Neolithic take on your Museum Secretorum, since &quot;one way or another, it has always existed&quot;. I have to wonder, though, whether they are a tradition that would have originated from the Vinca. Or, like the <i>Gudthabak</i>, they hail from a different culture/people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the Hototogisu, so if there is a way to add them into the setting I won't say no :P<br /> <br /> Do you mean for the Museum as a part of the Trader caste? I can see how it works. If there is a group which would collect strange things is that one. Not sure if they already put Wise into amber, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T00:31:39-07:00","id":925780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=925584#post925584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, regarding the Knights, it's likely they keep their own workings secret and it's probably not impossible for them to discover the secret murders the Wise are committing. The average mortal likely wouldn't simply because they're homebodies, while Knights are wandering warriors.<br /> <br /> And while the Tower of Babel and Nimrod are possibly after the Vinca times, in the Dark Era there's explicitly a 'Tower of Babel' like plothook involving an idigam.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I can see it works for the Knights.<br /> <br /> As for Nimrod and the Tower of Babel- well, that's the territory of the &quot;rule of cool&quot; I believe. If you have a good idea to add Nimrod to the setting, then why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T02:43:51-07:00","id":925807,"title":"","content":"I think the traders would make good cover for the Knights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T07:24:57-07:00","id":925885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=925807#post925807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the traders would make good cover for the Knights.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Though I imagine the majority of them are hunters who have abandoned their former villages and live in the wilds.<br /> <br /> For a Neolithic version of the Museum Secretorum, maybe they haven't learned how to encase Awakened in amber prisons. But perhaps they might employ a ritual which renders the Wise they capture comatose, and their magic is somehow channeled from them through their soul stones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 07-04-2016, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T07:44:25-07:00","id":925892,"title":"","content":"I think it'd depend on the strategy. The hunter knights are going to have to wait until the Wise venture out into the wilds (which they clearly do, so it's not a terrible idea). The Trader Knights would be able to actually infiltrate Vinca society which woud allow them take the offensive against the Wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T11:57:16-07:00","id":926547,"title":"","content":"Just to remember that Traders are all being suspected by the Vinca communities by general because everything that comes out of the wilderness could be a threat- and there is no bigger threat tot he community than killing its Wise. That would mean that those Knights who use being Trader as a cover are either the best at what they do, or that they are highly suicidal and willing to sacrifice their life in the process. Most likely? both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T12:59:10-07:00","id":926579,"title":"","content":"Sorry, that was kinda my point. They both have merits.<br /> <br /> Though, actually it's not like the Vinca really have the idea of fortrification yet. The hunter Knights probably could just rock up to the Wise's hut and attack them before the rest of the village can do much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T13:51:19-07:00","id":926612,"title":"","content":"I didn't said they won't manage to kill the Wise- the question is if they'll manage to get out alive. They are still going to have an angry mob going after them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T14:35:28-07:00","id":926641,"title":"","content":"It's probably easier to skip town if you're a hunter than a trader. I mean, a trader relies on hospitality and social networks; everytime you kill a wise you basically have to start over again as you're effectively burning your social network, plus other traders aren't going to be happy with you giving them a bad name.<br /> <br /> Even if you're stealthy, people are going to notice the trail of dead wizards eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T14:37:41-07:00","id":926644,"title":"","content":"yeah, that sounds quit how it should be","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T02:18:43-07:00","id":926938,"title":"","content":"ammut post 1<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-22-2016, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T03:27:47-07:00","id":926962,"title":"","content":"well, I've wrote that big and awesome post about To the Strongest with hunter organizations from Greece, Persia, India, Mesopotamia and Phoenicia, but the forums has turned into Ammut mode and devoured it whole, leaving me with only the sum up of the Neolithic Era...<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lighting the Candle/Primal State of </u></b><b><u>Grace</u></b><br /> <b>- The Wolf Hunter Cult</b> (the Nibiru, Hunter Caste. Those wolf masked dancers travel the wilderness both physical and spiritual and bind dangerous gods to deathlike sleep while maintaining harmony between the worlds)<br /> <b>-The Heart Breakers</b> (Knights of St George, barbarian warriors who live outside the community. They believe the Omphalos Stones and the Wise to be destructive influence over the community and fight their influence, and by doing so they drew the attention of something from the wilds)<br /> <b>-The Shield and Spear</b> (Aegis Kai Doru, Potter Caste. They are crafters and artificers who serve as the Wise's guardians both in the community and on the wilderness travels. Thanks to a special rite using the Omphalos Stones, they become ember bearers with the ability to use magical relics no mortal man should)<br /> -<b>The Marauders</b> (Promethean Brotherhood, fallen communities who lost their Wise and were given a special rite by an unknown force. Thanks to the ritual, they can steal the Wisdom of others and protect their own villiges)<br /> <b>- The </b><b>Forest</b><b> Travelers</b> (Museum Secretorum, Trader Caste. Those individuals risk their body and soul by travelling into the wilds and search for exotic resources and raw materials for their own communities and Wise and trade them with each other) <br /> <b>-The Grave Stricken </b>(either Cainte Heresy or pre-Kigal Ebony Fangs, for Kigal would be destroyed around the time of Irem. Outcasts who were touched or harmed by the dead, making them to be treated as dead by themselves. They are the ones to preform burial rites who keep loved ones from returning, and deal with them when they do)<br /> <b>Potential Plot Hooks-</b> Romohals, Nimrod in the Tower, Mistress of Honey (either Bird or some Underworld horror), packs of Cannibal Slashers<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T07:17:52-07:00","id":927033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=926962#post926962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, I've wrote that big and awesome post about To the Strongest with hunter organizations from Greece, Persia, India, Mesopotamia and Phoenicia, but the forums has turned into Ammut mode and devoured it whole, leaving me with only the sum up of the Neolithic Era...</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn...<br /> <br /> Here's me hoping you can remake it. But in the meantime, I am liking these brief write-ups. I'd probably go with the Grave Stricken being pre-Kigal Ebony Fangs, especially since their Endowment works nicely for the era.<br /> <br /> I got another question. How would you reskin the <i>Maagal</i> for the Sundered World?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T07:49:55-07:00","id":927055,"title":"","content":"Ammut post number 2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-07-2016, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T07:56:12-07:00","id":927058,"title":"","content":"well, wow- what the hell? I've once more made the post, and once more it was eaten by the forums. Thankfully, this time I have a back up, which I'll post later. Maybe it is just too big? :P<br /> <br /> As for the Maagal- they are not going to be present among the Vinca. During those times, they are among those Sekhem Sorcerers who sit in Canaan who will be conquered by the Shaniatu, so they need to be geographically close to them- so the Halaf Culture would be more appropriate. Their community would also be Wise-less, since their old artifice allows them to use the blessings of the gods without them being around, making it so the Sundering won't effect them so much.<br /> <br /> Also, I do agree that the Ebony Fangs works thematically with the all &quot;exiled from society&quot; thing- however, they are supposed to get their Endowments only after the the travel in the Underworld (not to mention it is an ocean right now). However, maybe at least some parts of the Words would work for them- Laws would not be appropriate, but maybe Names would?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-06-2016, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T08:12:43-07:00","id":927069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=927058#post927058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Maagal- they are not going to be present among the Vinca. During those times, they are among those Sekhem Sorcerers who sit in Canaan who will be conquered by the Shaniatu, so they need to be geographically close to them- so the Halaf Culture would be more appropriate. Their community would also be Wise-less, since their old artifice allows them to use the blessings of the gods without them being around, making it so the Sundering won't effect them so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=927058#post927058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I do agree that the Ebony Fangs works thematically with the all &quot;exiled from society&quot; thing- however, they are supposed to get their Endowments only after the the travel in the Underworld (not to mention it is an ocean right now). However, maybe at least some parts of the Words would work for them- Laws would not be appropriate, but maybe Names would?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Probably. And would that make the Grave Stricken the reverse of the modern day Fangs in terms of Endowments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T08:30:14-07:00","id":927082,"title":"","content":"yep- after all, during that time they are a rising conspiracy, while in modern time they are fallen one. Such reflection is important, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T08:34:39-07:00","id":927086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=926962#post926962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, I've wrote that big and awesome post about To the Strongest with hunter organizations from Greece, Persia, India, Mesopotamia and Phoenicia, but the forums has turned into Ammut mode and devoured it whole, leaving me with only the sum up of the Neolithic Era...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I every post longer than one or two paragraphs write as DOC or ODT file to paste into Post Reply... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-06-2016, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T08:37:55-07:00","id":927090,"title":"","content":"that's what I usually do, and I had a bad feeling before that- but I said &quot;nah- what are the chances?&quot; :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T10:59:33-07:00","id":927170,"title":"","content":"once more, trying to post To the Strongest:<br /> <br /> To The Strongest takes place after a big leap of time since the previous Dark Era. During that moment, many different cultures clash together, creating the foundation for not only the magical society, but to the Western Culture in general. The effect of Alexander's conquests shakes old traditions and establish new ones, and the terata, those monsters wearing human mask, spread through the empire beyond their native lands, infecting one nation after the other with their presence. When the shadows stir, the vigilantes take stand- yet each of the many countries united by Alexander has its own ideas about the Vigil, and while they have a common enemy no one promised that they would work together for that goal.<br /> <br /> First, we have Greece. The heart of the empire has formed a wide range of organizations; each is dedicated to hunting down the monsters that lurk in the night. The Aegis Kai Doru has already took into shape a lot like their modern incarnation. The Collega Chironos (name by Glamourweaver) are formed from free slaves who know the secrets of medicine and how to use beasts in order to make men into heroes. The<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/504497-museum-secretorum-witch-finder-conspiracy\"> Museum Secretorum </a>may only be established during the Late Antiquity, yet its foundations of collecting mysteries and discovering new wonders are already being formed. The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/638207-garden-of-the-hesperides-dream-catchers\">Garden of Hesperides</a> travels the kingdoms of the gods and collects stolen ambrosia and nectar to heal the sick and save souls. Many mystery cults take place in those lands, from the Orphic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/848708-pomegranate-deme-graverobbers-project-o-x-ix\">Pomegranate Deme </a>who trap the dead in little boxes, through the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/695939-the-civil-war-when-conspiracies-fall?p=913350#post913350\">Tenders of Dionysian Vineyard</a> who use wine and ecstasy to walk as gods and up to the dark Mysteries of Hecate who use the Rite of the Crossroad to steal light not their own, and that without mentioning the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/692793-conspiracy-order-of-the-void\">Order of the Nameless</a>, and heresy of hedge witches who follow a philosopher who never was in quest for power. Sparta alone stand apart of the grand empire, and as such it may have developed its own Vigil to protect itself from both supernatural and mundane threats.<br /> <br /> However, there are other nations in the Empire and their Vigil as such as ancient and powerful- if not more. In Egypt, the Cult of Set has already fallen into ruin, leaving the Cult of the Phoenix to burn in both day and night as the Ascending Ones. The Faithful of Shulpae have fed upon the rotting corpses of their own gods for years, and they yearn for the fresh blood of stranger divinities. The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/507852-the-temple-of-silence-cosnpiracy\">Temple of Silence</a> keeps singing its old requiem, keeping the graves of the dead undisturbed and untouched. The<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/600502-maw-of-the-river-mummy-hunters\"> Maw of the River</a> hunger for new wonders, and they follow the gifts of the River through the grant civilization in order to bring them back to the past. The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/862223-eye-of-heavens-tombraiders-project-x-o-vi\">Eye of Heaven</a> has already been formed from the desperate cults of the Serpent and the Vulture, and while they still lack their divine Mandate the libraries of their country hide many secrets about the future, as they wait to see who is the one to become king.<br /> <br /> Persia and India do not fall behind in their own Vigil- in the former Achaemenid Empire, the Taftani (temp name) weave heavenly fire into form which they channel through crafted artifacts to banish the Lie, while the immortal Anusiya (Glamourweaver thought about the concept) burn their own blood into light. In India, the weapons of the gods are carried by the Astradhari to battle hidden demons and monsters, while the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/605707-aga-nritya-dark-era-the-thuggee-cult\">Aga Nritya</a> dance an heretic dance in the name of Kali and Shiva. The Levant and Mesopotamia also don't fall behind- between the two rivers, even the proud Nibiru has bowed their head, learning from past mistakes as their nine lines go through Alexander's empire and keep old gods in deathlike sleep. The Su (Ebony Fangs) lurk outside the great cities and wondrous places, traveling as exiles while putting the many restless dead left behind Alexander's conquest back to rest. As they travel, Ereshkigal changes her name and face, adapting with their syncretistic faith- in Greece, she is Persephone, in India- Kali, and in Egypt she was always known as Ammut. Beyond those countries, in the Holy Land itself, the foundations for both <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/16573-conspiracy-raziel-ltd-wip\">Raziel Ltd</a> and Hakollel Shel HaMerkava (by Kingsraven) are being laid, although in way unrecognizable by their modern incarnations.<br /> <br /> The coasts of Phoenicia have also seen their own share of hunters and monsters through the ages- yet all has changed when Alexander crushed them with iron fist. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/584777-maagal-habaal-vehaashera-dark-eras-book-of-judges\">Maagal HaBaal VeHaAshera</a> was shattered together with Tyr, and its broken remains were gathered together in Carthage- but while the city would flourish, its old nemesis would make sure it would never return to its former glory. Phoenician Sailors (who may or may not be connected to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571472-navio-de-tolos-beast-hunters\">Navio de Tolos</a>) has shifted their interest from Tyr to the New City, searching for new adventures and hidden mysteries beyond the sea. Still, one group has its control over Carthage hunters more than any other- the drums may have been silenced in the Levant, but they are heard strongly in the New City, as the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/739877-cult-of-moloch-convention\">Cult of Moloch</a> keeps on burning in those lands.<br /> <br /> Yes, man has formed a great Vigil for- but he is not the only one to light the candle. Demons hold it too. While the blood of Lucifer would only come during the days of the late Roman Empire, other <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/866426-strains-of-the-cursed-blood\">strains of the cursed blood</a> are already present, who may or may not be connected to those future royals of hell. En has already fell in Babylon by the hands of the Edimmu, and their ritual was already preformed by the hands of mortals- calling a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/893684-al-rih-al-asuad-strains-of-the-cursed-blood-mesopotamia\">Black Wind</a> to blow through the land and banish lesser demons by Pazuzu's name. Centuries ago, a snake-like demon has awakened from its sleep beneath Egypt's red desert, and those who survived its venom were marked by chaos for all eternity. In Greece, those who were born from the Erinyes punish wicked mortals who defy the rules of both men and gods. In Persia, the offspring of the Usij fight the Lie in their own way, knowing that as being forever tainted by blood they are allowed to perform acts others are not able to. In India, sinners are being reincarnated as Asura in a form of punishment for their former lives, and now they are forced to redeem themselves for the next cycle. And every where the fires of Moloch have burned, children were given to the inferno- and those who passed through the flames unharmed harness that tainted power against their own parents and priesthood under the name of Benei Tofet.<br /> <br /> Yes, those are wild times, and no one knows what would happen next. As monsters and men meet together and turn upon each other, as Alexander falls in war engulfs his empire, only one thing is certain- that empire and its shattered remain would only belong to one. To the strongest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-06-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T01:16:24-07:00","id":927487,"title":"","content":"Interesting write-up there. Will comment more when I got time.<br /> <br /> P.S: It looks like the forums kicked themselves out of Ammut mode and spat out your other attempts ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T01:33:02-07:00","id":927491,"title":"","content":"damn Shuankshen :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T02:00:46-07:00","id":928652,"title":"","content":"after giving it some thought, I came to the conclusion that the potential Phoenician sailors group would not be connected by any way to the Navio de Tolos- the Navio are, by design, based around the ideas of the Age of Discovery and Portugal's role in it, drawing a lot of inspiration from the time and the place. Forcing the two groups together would be a bit forced and harm both the feeling of the existing conspiracy and the potential outcome of the future one. In sort, I've decided to let the Navio stay the Navio and seek for a different, independent idea for the Phoenician group which could have carried on to modern time, apparently being based around trade in some way.<br /> <br /> Still trying to think about ideas for the Spartan group","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T16:02:17-07:00","id":928933,"title":"","content":"<b>Note:</b> Why don't you just change name of topic on something like <i>Hunter's Dark Eras</i>? It's a bit confusing name as it is...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=928652#post928652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">after giving it some thought, I came to the conclusion that the potential Phoenician sailors group would not be connected by any way to the Navio de Tolos- the Navio are, by design, based around the ideas of the Age of Discovery and Portugal's role in it, drawing a lot of inspiration from the time and the place. Forcing the two groups together would be a bit forced and harm both the feeling of the existing conspiracy and the potential outcome of the future one. In sort, I've decided to let the Navio stay the Navio and seek for a different, independent idea for the Phoenician group which could have carried on to modern time, apparently being based around trade in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe some Sea Serpents appesers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=928652#post928652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still trying to think about ideas for the Spartan group</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe based those on <i>300</i> comic, where Spartiats need to come to age by defeating 'monstrous' wolf? Spartan group could trying to repeat this feat over and over again, with more demanding monsters, as means to prove themselves. Hell, they could even have werewolves ( in Urshul form ) as favored prey! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HSvBr4Qa-Fs\" data-code=\"HSvBr4Qa-Fs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HSvBr4Qa-Fs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T06:17:23-07:00","id":929212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=928933#post928933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Note:</b> Why don't you just change name of topic on something like <i>Hunter's Dark Eras</i>? It's a bit confusing name as it is...</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really like the name- and besides, the project is meant to include other possible historic settings, like Sothis Ascends or Requiem for Rome. Plus, the idea behind this project is to make it less like Dark Eras (with which includes a full and well detailed setting) and more like Ancient Mysteries/Bloodlines (who touch certain Eras and give some new options), so a different name for a different function.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe some Sea Serpents appesers? </div> </div> </div>I don't know- sounds too &quot;culty&quot;, and I think that &quot;conquering the Sea&quot; is more in their theme than &quot;appeasing it&quot;. I think they should have some Lovecraftian themes, with connection to Mummy and some Levaithan sidebars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe based those on <i>300</i> comic, where Spartiats need to come to age by defeating 'monstrous' wolf? Spartan group could trying to repeat this feat over and over again, with more demanding monsters, as means to prove themselves. Hell, they could even have werewolves ( in Urshul form ) as favored prey! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HSvBr4Qa-Fs\" data-code=\"HSvBr4Qa-Fs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HSvBr4Qa-Fs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div> </div> </div> </div>never heard about this comic or saw 300 (well, I saw the parody, but it doesn't count, right?). Is it based around real origin myth? If not, making them as werewolf hunter could still be interesting, but would require another justification. Maybe by focusing on their themes of &quot;personal excellence&quot; and &quot;becoming the best warrior&quot; by challenging the lords of the Shadows and those known as the &quot;best hunters&quot;?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T23:42:03-07:00","id":929585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=929212#post929212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">never heard about this comic or saw 300 (well, I saw the parody, but it doesn't count, right?). Is it based around real origin myth? If not, making them as werewolf hunter could still be interesting, but would require another justification. Maybe by focusing on their themes of &quot;personal excellence&quot; and &quot;becoming the best warrior&quot; by challenging the lords of the Shadows and those known as the &quot;best hunters&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just read comic - it's what most Eastern RPGer think about Sparta in the end. When making Spartan hunters you will need to at least acknowlegde how it's differ from <i>300</i>. Movie is a bit weaker, but has butiful images. And parody it terrible - just read/watch original.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T02:50:18-07:00","id":929634,"title":"","content":"I don't know- when designing a new hunter group, I usually prefer to rely on historic/mythological base over something from pop-culture, so I don't know how much I like the concept of adapting that fiction, especially since I'm not that familiar with it. That <a href=\"http://www.ancientgreekbattles.net/Pages/90073_SpartaWolf.htm\" target=\"_blank\">webstie</a>, however, claims that there is a Sparta-wolf connection which sounds very interesting to explore (especially since they also add Apollo to the equation- so Apollo the Sun Wolf everyone!), and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crypteia\" target=\"_blank\">Crypteia </a>also sounds like a good base for an hunter group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T02:19:28-07:00","id":930248,"title":"","content":"I'm going to post the ideas for the next Era (Three Kingdoms of Darkness) later today, so here is a sum up of everything we have until now.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lighting the Candle/Primal State of </u></b><b><u>Grace</u></b><br /> <b>-</b><b> The Wolf Hunter Cult</b> (the Nibiru, Hunter Caste. Those wolf masked dancers travel the wilderness both physical and spiritual and bind dangerous gods to deathlike sleep while maintaining harmony between the worlds)<br /> <b>-The Heart Breakers</b> (Knights of St George, barbarian warriors who live outside the community. They believe the Omphalos Stones and the Wise to be destructive influence over the community and fight their influence, and by doing so they drew the attention of something from the wilds)<br /> <b>-The Shield and Spear</b> (Aegis Kai Doru, Potter Caste. They are crafters and artificers who serve as the Wise's guardians both in the community and on the wilderness travels. Thanks to a special rite using the Omphalos Stones, they become ember bearers with the ability to use magical relics no mortal man should)<br /> -<b>The Marauders</b> (Promethean Brotherhood, fallen communities who lost their Wise and were given a special rite by an unknown force. Thanks to the ritual, they can steal the Wisdom of others and protect their own villiges)<br /> <b>- The </b><b>Forest</b><b> Travelers</b> (Museum Secretorum, Trader Caste. Those individuals risk their body and soul by travelling into the wilds and search for exotic resources and raw materials for their own communities and Wise and trade them with each other)<br /> <b>-The Grave Stricken </b>(pre-Kigal Ebony Fangs. Outcasts who were touched or harmed by the dead, making them to be treated as dead by themselves. They are the ones to preform burial rites who keep loved ones from returning, and deal with them when they do)<br /> <b>Potential Plot Hooks-</b> Romohals, Nimrod in the Tower, Mistress of Honey (either Bird or some Underworld horror), packs of Cannibal Slashers<br /> <br /> <b><u>Army of Sheep/Kings and Barbarians</u></b><br /> <b>-Aegis Kai Doru</b> (Greece, collectors of ancient relics who hunt witches and werewolves for ancient treason against men and gods)<br /> <b>-Collega Chironos</b> (Greece, freed slaves who use their knowledge of medicine to heal the sick and use beasts to make men into heroes)<br /> <b>-Kruptos Syllogi</b> (Greece, note me if my Greek didn't came out well. They are the traders and elites of the empire, inspired to collect the many wonders seen through Alexander's conquests)<br /> <b>-Garden of Hesperides </b>(Greece, small mystery cult who walk into the garden of the gods to find healing herbs and save souls who were lost in the Garden)<br /> -<b>Pomegranate Deme</b> (Greece, Orphic cult who trap dead souls in pyxis in order to enrich themselves in the next life and preserve their knowledge)<br /> <b>-Tenders of the Dionysian Vineyard</b> (Greece, Les Mysteres. Part of the Dionysian Mysteries who use wine and ecstasy to walk as gods among men)<br /> -<b>Mysteries of Hecate</b> (Greece, Promethean Brotherhood. astrologers who worship the goddess of witchcraft and steal the light from the unworthy tyrants)<br /> <b>-Order of the Nameless</b> (Greece, philosophers inspired by stolen secrets of Babylon who follow a wise man who never was)<br /> <b>-Lycos Agema </b>(Greece, elite Spartan soldiers chosen among the Crypteia who hunt werewolves and other monsters as part of their martial excellence)<br /> <b>-Pyr Tartarus</b> (Greece, children of the Erinyes who punish wicked people who break the laws of men and gods)<br /> <b>-Ascending Ones</b> (Egypt, alchemist who transform poison into power through faith and fight against undead abominations)<br /> <b>-Faithful of Shulpae</b> (Egypt, old cult who worship their gods by eating them and gaining their divinity and now spread through the empire)<br /> <b>-Temple of Silence </b>(Egypt, a cult of Nephthys who maintain the proper burial of the dead and protect their graves)<br /> <b>-Maw of the River</b> (Egypt, relic hunters who worship Sobek as they destroy old artifacts of the past and follow an old form of justice)<br /> <b>-Eye of Heaven</b> (Egypt, advisers and oracles who guide the future leaders to the right path in shaping history)<br /> <b>-Hrt Isfet</b> (Egypt, descendants of those who survived Apep's venom and lived who are cursed by Chaos for all eternity)<br /> <b>-Taftani</b> (Persia, crafters who weave Ahura Mazda's holy fire into items of power and use them as weapon against Ahriman's slaves)<br /> <b>-Anusiya</b> (Persia, elite warriors who burn their own blood into divine light to banish the horrors which hide from the sun)<br /> <b>-Usij</b> (Persia, priests of the Lie who are ridden by evil thoughts who use that taint as a weapon and shield when fighting demons)<br /> <b>-Astradhari</b> (India, warriors who carry the mystical weapons of the gods forged by strange metals in their battle against monsters)<br /> <b>-Chakravanti</b> (India, Aga Nritya. Heretic death cult who believe in advancing in Wheel and sending both monsters and sinners to their next life for their own good)<br /> <b>-Asurendra</b> (India, sinners in their previous life reincarnated as demons who seek to redeem themselves for their next cycle by fighting monsters)<br /> <b>-Nibiru</b> (Mesopotamia, lineage of women mystics who maintain the bindings of ancient gods through Alexander's empire)<br /> <b>-Su</b> (Mesopotamia, Ebony Fangs. Necromancers and mediums who live in the shadows of the empire as exiles and banish the dead)<br /> <b>-Saru Salmu </b>(Mesopotamia, al Rih al Asuad. Children of Pazuzu invoked through ancient ritual to fight against vampires and other demons of the night)<br /> <b>-Shoftim</b> (Levant, Hakollel Shel HaMerkava. Jewish priests who guide their people in the holy land and fight against monsters with names of divine fire)<br /> <b>-Benei HaOr</b> (Levant, Raziel Ltd. Jewish cult who crave holy verses into weapons using ancient scrolls in the war of the Sons of Light against the Sons of Dark)<br /> <b>-Maagal HaBaal VeHaAshera</b> (Phoenicia, once a proud conspiracy of idol makers who gave life to their gods, their shattered remains hide in Carthage)<br /> <b>-Adonei HaYam</b> (Phoenicia, sailors and traders who cross the sea upon ships, fighting the primordial horrors on their path and trade in pure lifeforce)<br /> <b>-Cult of Moloch</b> (Phoenicia, priests who worship a principle of love and sacrifice who burn their own children for glory, based in Carthage)<br /> <b>-Benei Tophet</b> (Phoenicia, few chosen children who survive the fires of Moloch and turn upon their priesthood and parents in fighting the ancient demons)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-12-2016, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T03:57:59-07:00","id":930269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=927170#post927170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sparta alone stand apart of the grand empire, and as such it may have developed its own Vigil to protect itself from both supernatural and mundane threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only for about 7 years. Alexander eventually forced them to join the League of Corinth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T04:11:19-07:00","id":930273,"title":"","content":"Well, Greek history is not my specialty, so I just used the Dark Eras book as my base which detailed Sparta as &quot;technically independent, yet irrelevant&quot;, and my interpretation may have been flawed because of that. Still, the main difference between Sparta and Athens makes sense that each created its own Vigil culture, and with the Aegis Kai Doru being based in the later Sparta deserve some group of its own. Of course, Alexander and his father's conquest did influenced the idea of &quot;we are all Greeks&quot;- but old traditions don't die out quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T04:43:50-07:00","id":930281,"title":"","content":"Technically all the city states are independent. Philip and Alexander are merely the leaders of the League.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd think the AKD would probably be in both cities. Networks of Greek aristocrats weren't restricted to individual city states. I mean, a lot of what we know of Spartan culture comes from Athenian aristocrats who had friends in Sparta.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a Spartan tradition for inspiration, I'd look up the Crypteia. There's some dispute over how real it was, but the idea at least is that annually young Spartan men would be sent out into the countryside at night to attack the Helot population (basically the serfs). That sounds not totally unlike a vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T04:49:06-07:00","id":930282,"title":"","content":"yep, the Crypteia would be used as a source of inspiration for them- that is, if and when I'll manage to write them. My to-do list is already as long as the Great Wall of China :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T05:59:41-07:00","id":930292,"title":"","content":"so- about the Three Kingdoms of Darkness:<br /> <br /> The time of the Three Kingdoms is a violent Era. People fight and die in the name of heroism, as warlords wage war against one another. There is a reason why the hunters of the Era are described as &quot;bands of brothers&quot; tied by bonds stronger than blood. The Mandate of Heaven rules above all, and those who serve it thrive while those who abuse it fall. That civil war is not done for one's own sake- but in the name of Heaven, and people do some terrible thing in the name of personal survival and heroism as long as it may be justified by the Mandate. In many ways, such an era of selfish heroism could describe as one of the aspects of what an hunter must deal with during the Vigil- and that takes it to the extreme. Even in modern times hunters wonder how far the Vigil takes them- just where the lines are crossed? Just when something is right or wrong? Using the Vigil as a justification for one's own terrible deeds is how most of the hunters survive today- but now, if that Vigil is not just a man-made concept but is a duty granted by Heaven itself, who are you to judge yourself for actions Heaven decreed that must be done? Yes, this is a violent time, heroic time and a very, very Vigilant Time.<br /> <br /> For the hunters of China, the Vigil means operating under the Mandate of Heaven- as long as your actions are done according to the will of above, you are just. Where modern hunters debt if killing a child witch is moral or not, the hunters of that Era may butcher an whole village and without blinking, mourning afterward for what they had to do in Heaven's name. This is a time of treachery, as people may betray one another in the name of personal gain- but hunters challenge that concept. The Vigil can't survive without trust- yet you can't truly have faith in anyone, forcing you to always sleep with one open eye.<br /> <br /> That Era has two, big players in the shadow world- Changeling and Sin Eaters. With the fall into a civil war, the ancient contracts and protections of the Lost are torn apart, allowing the Huntsmen to flood the land, yet they keep following the Mandate of Heaven as their heroic story tell itself. With so many dead with regrets being left behind, someone has to put the souls back to rest- not to mention the many who seek for a second chance in life. Monsters wage war against one another under the cover of the personal battles and warring warlords- yet so many innocents are stuck in their way. Someone has to rise and put those monsters back in their place, for this is their role under the Mandate.<br /> <br /> With China being separated from the world Alexander has shaped, we can be sure that no familiar face would show up in that land- but there are others who would take their place. The Shi (converted by Reighnhell) seem to have been around since the time of the Shang Dynasty- and while the civil war tears the whole world apart the mystical monks did survived. The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/695939-the-civil-war-when-conspiracies-fall?p=913350#post913350\">Tianxia Order </a>talks with spirits and gods under the Mandate's authority and make sure the Shadow would follow Heaven's decree. The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/404571-semi-comapct-theater-of-tragedies\">Theater of Tragedies</a> also exist in that Era under the guise of the Wu Keng, a classic example of search after selfish glory as they make pacts with the demons who defy the Mandate- only to betray them later. With versions of both the Wu Nung and the Wu Keng around, a translation for the Wu Lung is also expected, as those chosen by the dragons pull the strings of Fate and commune directly with the Mandate of Heaven through sacred bureaucracy and holy laws written in calligraphy, targeting Yaoguai and their agents. Talking about the Yaoguai, this is also an opportunity to present another Strain of Cursed blood- the beast shifters descendant from the Fae of China, who hunt after those who are touched by their demonic influence. With so many dead, the world is out of harmony- and those who work with the mediums of the land are a Taoist group who use the eight point diagram in order to being the world back to its natural state and clean the taint of death. While I would have loved tying both the Red Envelope Society (by Caitiff Primogen) and Hotel Mascaron (be Reviled) to the Era, both would originate only during the Tang Dynsaty- but maybe some of Reviled's other ideas which are detailed in the Hotel writeup could be developed, as detailed bellow:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">the reincarnation police of the Avichi Sutra and their obliterative mudras, the kukri-wielding soldiers who make up the Royal Kauda Corps, the anarchistic sorcerers called the Seven Wanton Horns, the gangsters of the Diyu Tong who cover themselves in squirming tattoos, the ritualistic thugs of the Feringhea Phansigar, the penniless master-killers known as the Guild of Assassins, the psychomanifesting spirit hunters trained by the Extranormal Society for Special Execution, the loyal communist investigators of the Wang Jun Xiu, the Taoist arms dealers dedicated to the Blood Principle, and more besides.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Some are of course too modern for the Era- yet we could undoubtedly expect some to show up, and that is without mentioning which hunters did the people of the steppe brought with them.</span><br /> <br /> This is an Era of war, heroism, treachery and survival.<br /> <br /> There is not better time to uphold the Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T12:11:47-07:00","id":930460,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm trying to think how to adapt the Gem Cutters from the old Phoenix: the Risen project to &quot;To The Strongest&quot; Era. I did liked that project, and if I remember it right their origin was Greek. Maybe as Beast or Spirit hunters of some kind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T04:48:29-07:00","id":931273,"title":"","content":"A <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ofn43jnpTpDh_c7Lqky2l5d8KvaeDH1Lq-QH1oX5uZ8/edit\" target=\"_blank\">draft </a>for both the Nibiru and the Heartbreakers of the Neolithic. Say what you think","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 11-12-2018, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T09:56:03-07:00","id":931424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=931273#post931273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QS8oJsZ2d2bpyKMwjTbwQXblL5q59LSvLGCfvXay2Ys/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">draft </a>for both the Nibiru and the Heartbreakers of the Neolithic. Say what you think</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the usual grammar errors here and there (and the fact that I've seen the Nibiru write-up before), they're all pretty good descriptions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Can't wait for the rest, though I am sorely tempted to try my hand at a write-up on the Shield and Spear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:16:02-07:00","id":931437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=931424#post931424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aside from the usual grammar errors here and there (and the fact that I've seen the Nibiru write-up before), they're all pretty good descriptions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Can't wait for the rest, though I am sorely tempted to try my hand at a write-up on the Shield and Spear.</div> </div> </div> </div>feel free to do so! this is an Open Invite, after all :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T19:01:10-07:00","id":932729,"title":"","content":"<u><b>The Shield and Spear - Guardians of the Wise</b></u><br /> <br /> Having braved the Supernal World to Awaken to their lost birthright, the Wise stand as champions of the People against the shadows that lurk beyond the light of the hearthfires. Each speaks on her village's behalf to the spirits that are deeply intertwined with their way of life, and each is ready to work magic alongside her Circle to fight those who would prey upon the People.<br /> <br /> But even the Wise cannot stand alone for long.<br /> <br /> As they carry out their duties and pursue their Mysteries, the Wise are beset by enemies on all sides. Spirits roam the Land in abundance, quick to kill or Ride any who approach them in ignorance (or, worse, arrogance). Uratha emerge from the wilds to raid villages, seeing their residents as nothing but prey to their fangs and claws. And as the world trembles with their coming, even the gods themselves may turn on the People in pursuit of their own goals.<br /> <br /> The Wise must also watch for more mundane dangers. They find themselves increasingly at odds with the hunter-cults of their communities, and barbarian outcasts who shun their protection out of fear of their power. The latter group works to undo everything they have built by slaying the Awakened priests of the village and - if possible - shattering the god-hearts in every village they plague.<br /> <br /> Faced with such numerous threats, and in spite of the powers they wielded, the Wise would have fallen long ago on their own. However, even before the Bird and the Bull gave their gifts, they came to rely upon several of the People for aid. These men and women lived free of the Sleeping Curse's touch. Their souls were not truly illuminated with Awakening, but they could bear witness to the magics of the Wise without succumbing to madness or the fogging of memories. These &quot;ember bearers&quot;, as the People called them, were therefore valued not only as assistants and acolytes, but also as guardians and protectors.<br /> <br /> When the People prospered from the blessing of the Omphalos Stones, the Cult of the Shield and Spear was formed from the most dedicated ember bearers among them. These dauntless individuals swore binding oaths before the Omphalos Stones, pledging to defend the Wise from the many dangers that would lead to their fall. And in the pursuit of this task, they were armed not just with the hearth magics of their villages, but vessels blessed with pure Supernal fire as well.<br /> <br /> The Shield and Spear faithfully carried out their duties for generations. They have guarded the Circles of the Wise in their journeys, clashing with spirits, werewolves, and even those among humankind who saw their charges as enemies. Some would even sacrifice their lives to ensure the Awakened safely returned to the villages. So great was their loyalty to the Wise that they came to earn their own place of honor among the People.<br /> <br /> Recently, though, the cult has had its faith shaken. Its members accompanied the Wise in their quests to seek new Omphalos Stones from the gods, and many took part in the battle that ended with Fox's death. They find themselves complicit in the Lie given to the People, even as the gods withdraw their favor and grow more hostile with each divinity murdered by the Wise. Most continue to stand with their Awakened champions, convinced that their actions are for the greater good of their communities.<br /> <br /> Yet as the world begins to change, as the violence of war plagues several villages and bull-shifters migrate from the east, some begin to fear they must act before all that they know is destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 07-17-2016, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T19:56:43-07:00","id":932749,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a>, interesting, but couple of thoughts on write-up.<br /> <br /> 1. Can there even be 'Shield and Spear'? Based on documentaries <b>Stories From Stone Age </b>( appropriate part is <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eWLbQjbqGfs\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, Vinca culture starts at 1:50 in it - but I advise to watch whole series ) I thought that weapons were not done at least till 2000 BCE. Even if spears would be, shields almost surely would not be in time of Vinca culture.<br /> <br /> 2. You need to lost modern terms - in<i> Sundered World</i> Era there were no Supernal, Awakened ( well, those could be, but I think I saw there was alternative to the term ) or even Sleeping Curse. Good would be to check names in Dark Eras chapter for proper names.<br /> <br /> Other than that - cool 'origins' of AKD Conspiracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-16-2016, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T22:23:06-07:00","id":932790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=932749#post932749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a>, interesting, but couple of thoughts on write-up.<br /> <br /> 1. Can there even be 'Shield and Spear'? Based on documentaries <b>Stories From Stone Age </b>( appropriate part is <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eWLbQjbqGfs\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, Vinca culture starts at 1:50 in it - but I advise to watch whole series ) I thought that weapons were not done at least till 2000 BCE. Even if spears would be, shields almost surely would not be in time of Vinca culture.<br /> <br /> 2. You need to lost modern terms - in<i> Sundered World</i> Era there were no Supernal, Awakened ( well, those could be, but I think I saw there was alternative to the term ) or even Sleeping Curse. Good would be to check names in Dark Eras chapter for proper names.<br /> <br /> Other than that - cool 'origins' of AKD Conspiracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit I did stumble a bit on the terms seeing as there are few (if any) alternative words I could use for them. And I did feel the name &quot;Shield and Spear&quot; seemed a bit out of place for the era. Perhaps something along the lines of <i>Cult of the Flame</i> or <i>Keepers of the Flame</i> might make more sense.<br /> <br /> That said, thanks for the feedback <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Will look at the video when I have the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T01:37:43-07:00","id":932841,"title":"","content":"I don't know about names involving Fire- sure, it is a symbol of civilization and Awakening, but it says nothing about their role as potters and artificers. I'm not sure about the exact timeline- but having items crafted by technology more advanced than the current timeline through Awakened/Spirituals knowledge should be almost like magic for the People, making such weapons into &quot;magic items&quot; (something like the Advanced Armory TF:V possess in the modern times). Calling themselves after the principle of their creation does not feel too &quot;inappropriate&quot;, I think<br /> <br /> 3 Kingdoms sort list-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Under the Mandate/Betraying the World</u></b><br /> <b>-Shi</b> (mystic monks who fight the influence of the Shen as they try to separate themselves from the civil war)<br /> <b>-Tianxia Order</b> (Les Mysteres, spiritual mediums who try to bring harmony to the Celestial Bureaucracy through sacred rites)<br /> <b>-Wu Keng</b> (heretic cult who use a twisted version of the cross dressing tradition to cheat both demons and the Mandate of Heaven)<br /> <b>-Wu Lung</b> (calligraphers who were granted the Mandate by dragons to make laws and try to rebuild their broken empire)<br /> <b>-Tianshang de Sunzi</b> (descendants of the Yaoguai who are masters of trickery and beast-shifitng and use their skills against their parents)<br /> <b>-Bagua</b> (taoist group who use the Eight Symbols in order to clean the taint of the death and return the world to its original state)<br /> <b>-Riders of Tengri</b> (hunters of the steppe who ride their horses as they hunt after the monsters of the plains)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-22-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T01:47:03-07:00","id":933782,"title":"","content":"ok, another week has passed- and this time, Vikings!<br /> <br /> The endless waves on invasion finally start to die out, and the nations of Europe finally dare to rise their head. The world starts to change, forcing the proud Northmen to either adapt or die out. Old traditions are destroyed as new ones take their place, and the northern pirates are slowly vanishing from the horizon. They stretched too much, they grew too much- and now, they fall under their own weight. However, while their glory in near its end, the story of the Vikings is not over yet. Through all of Europe, their presence was felt- and their legacy would carry own even after the wild times would end. For the hunters of Europe, the time represent both a danger and a opportunity- new lands are discovered, and new threats show their face. Some hunters would cling to their old ways when dealing with those new threats, while others embrace the new world and adapt to the upcoming changes. For years, the hunters of the Northmen rode the waves and fought the native monsters of the lands they took for themselves. They stood at the front of the fight, carrying the candle with pride and unwavering resolve. But as the Era comes to its end, the hunters become more and more tied to their local community- but the local hunters of the occupied lands won't forget the harms they suffered from them. And so, instead of working together against the monsters, it is more than likely that those hunters would leave each other to the dead.<br /> <br /> Still, for hunters, the main theme in this Era is exploration- new lands await for the brave, and the hunters would fight their way to Valhalla. The most basic fear always was the unknown, and those who dare to fight the monsters who hide in that darkness have their place promised as future warriors of the gods. They follow the footsteps of their own heroes, searching after giants and dragons and the dead who don't stay in their grave. Unlike the hunters of other nations, the Viking hunters has a complicated relationships with their own monsters- witches are to be scared of, but they are also respected. Werewolves are terrible enemies, but are also proud warriors. Sin eaters talk with the dead and guide souls to the halls of Hel and Valhalla. Vampires of a small clan known as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/405640-lost-clan-grettir\">Grettir </a>prey upon the Norsemen and doom them to exist as draugrs- but even those wild vampires has their uses. When the hunters of Scandinavia hunt their own monsters, they do so for glory and the chance to die honorably in battle- but when they hunt foreign monsters, it is to protect their people and gain the necessary resources for their people to survive. All hunters are warriors- but the hunters of the north are the greatest among their kind.<br /> <br /> The major players of the Era would be, of course, a Norse organization- and the Valdaermen (temp name) would fulfill that place. Carrying silver swords and covered with magical runes, the hunters of the conspiracy has traveled everywhere their ships has led them. Following the culture of their people, harsh divide of gender roles has left its mark upon the conspiracy, as the women of the group weave complicate runes to enchant the weapons and equipment of their people while the men use those weapons to fight monsters and other threats. There are two great enemies for those hunters- the dead and the werewolves, as the former being constant threat from souls who cling to their former lives and are try to escape their fate in Hel, while the others are seen as the spawn of Loki who would one day end the world. While the divide between the gender roles of the conspiracy is harsh, some dare to challenge it, gaining both the respect and loath of the rest of the group. Shieldmaidens storm the battle alongside the greatest warriors, while males are branded as Ergi for delving into the knowledge of sorcery. After years of controlling the northern sphere, as Christianity marches on the conspiracy would fall and die out- yet its secrets would remain carved into stones, waiting to be found by modern heirs of their glory.<br /> <br /> Those hunters, of course, are not the only ones around- with so many dead left to the cold winds and the Bound rising from their graves, you could be sure the Ebony Fangs would lurk around under the service of Hel, the half alive queen of the Underworld. As the Great Heathen Army rush through the lands of England, the current form of the Knights of St George would stand against their heretic witchcraft, as they start their tradition of using Christianity as a mask to their true nature, denying the existence of magic one hand and fighting its threat in the other. However, foreign witches are not their only target- for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/763228-shepherds-of-annwn-grave-robbers\">Shepherds of Annwn</a> travel the Welsh lands, being forced to hide from the Knights as they put the many restless dead to sleep so they won't call the Hounds of Hell. The Varangian Guard offers opportunities for not only the Uratha, but also for the hunters of Byzantium, becoming a power which would stand strong until the empire's upcoming fall. Frankia is now under the Carolingian dynasty's rule, and their own Vigil works more or less with harmony with the Norse hunters as they operate under the blessing of the Pope. Finally, against all chances, Dublin stood strong, unbowed by the endless invasions. However, it has its own problems- the slave trade is prospering, and the city was built unknowingly (probably) around a gate to the Underworld. The screams of the slaves echo into the dark pits, turning into a song which lures things from the pond better stay hidden. Some may think that this song has to be stopped- but others wish to harness its power to fight the monsters. For the Aided (temp name), the song of death is nothing modern, for they sang it by themselves for centuries- and if so many souls yearn for it, it is only fair to grant their wish.<br /> <br /> Ride the waves, fight the unknown and die in honor to enter Valhalla.<br /> <br /> This is what it means to be a hunter among Vikings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T00:57:17-07:00","id":935478,"title":"","content":"Something I've forgot about the Viking Era- during that time, the Museum Secretorum would have finally be established in its current form, and would finally change its focus from simply collecting strange phenomena into preserving knowledge as the Roman Empire falls to ruin and Europe enters the Dark Ages. They probably discovered the secrets of &quot;amber coating&quot; a witch during that time, becoming a proper conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T07:17:02-07:00","id":935588,"title":"","content":"Viking Era sort list<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Words of Praise/ Better Blind than Buried</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Valdaermen</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (gender divided organization who carry silver swords enchanted by rune by women and used to battle by men)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Howe Warders</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Ebony Fangs, groups of ergi and similar exiles who see themselves as Hel\u2019s beloved and send the dead to the afterlife)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Faceless Order</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Knights of St George, pagan witch hunters who start absorbing christian motifs as a masquerade for their Vigil)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Shepherds of Annwn</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Welsh blood witches who guard sacred places from both witches and the dead fearing ancient evil)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Ksirafai</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (shadowy watch of Byzantium who use the many Imperial Guards as a cover for their activities against monsters)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>-Sacre Calvaire</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(knights who style themselves after the 12 paladins and invoke divine powers for battle)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Aided</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (celtic death singers who are based around druidic tradition and call upon the dead to fight monsters)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T08:13:15-07:00","id":935610,"title":"","content":"so, some more thoughts about the Viking Era-<br /> <br /> after reading Tales of the Dark Era which gave a more in depth look for Beasts in the Viking time, I wonder who exactly should be the &quot;favorite enemies&quot; of the Valdaermen- Beasts are really interesting, and are supported by the Crossover Sidebar, but the image of hunters who carry rune carved silver swords and the shout out to Ascension with connecting them to the dead are just too awesome to give up on. Oh well- perhaps the &quot;Beast hunting&quot; aspect could be moved to one of the foreign groups.<br /> <br /> Talking about foreign groups- considering that the Byzantine Empire is in the background of the setting, the Aegis Kai Doru should also be in there. The Nibiru should also be around, travelling to the distant lands of Northern Europe as volvas and shamans. Also, since those are the Middle Ages, we can finally meet the Lucifuge who grew in the meanwhile among Western Europe, as the Pyr Tartarus take the guise of Eastern Orthodoxy (the Slavic Strain may also start forming in the Kievan Rus, but would still lack a solidified form).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T13:16:57-07:00","id":936687,"title":"","content":"some thoughts about After the Fall.<br /> <br /> Constantinople was a bastion of the God Machine's power, and with its fall the demons can finally attempt at building their own Hell. For the Unchained, this is a theme of hope- but for the regular people, this is Hell on Earth. The God Machine, while being a tyrant, was a stabilizing presence which kept the city- and the empire which evolved around it- under strict control. As God lost its grip over the city, all kinds of terrors are unleashed upon the citizens of the city- shadows lurk with hidden monsters, nightmares turn into truth. Vampires struggle over control, and innocent bystanders get caught in their struggle. Werewolves destroy the existing spirits ecology for better and worse. Terrible Undying Ones hide beneath the city and feast upon those who won't be missed. Witches and Reanimated are lured into Constantinople by the opportunities it offers. Nightmares take form and feast upon fear. The dead linger after the war. A slasher plunk the eyes of her victims as she move through the Underworld...<br /> <br /> And demons, demons everywhere.<br /> <br /> The themes of this Era are Rebuilding and Possibility- both for demons and for hunters. For years, everything was under control- but now, chaos spread through the shadow society, forcing the monolithic organizations of hunters to grow and change. There is a chance for profit in that situation- but the risk for failure could be terrible. With former conspiracies being reduced to ash, new groups has the opportunity to gain power and establish themselves in the Ottoman Empire. Others use the chaos in order to hunt their enemies and take over their resources. And of course, the Machine may have been watchful over the city bit it wasn't always kind- the God Machine works to preserve a status que, creating a mechanical Heaven with purpose for everything and few points of light in a sea of eternal darkness. While the destruction of its Infrastructures has unleashed countless horrors, it also gives the hunters an opportunity to challenge the laws of God and try to make a better world for themselves, creating their own Paradise which is free from both Heaven and Hell.<br /> <br /> Good luck with that.<br /> <br /> As for the main powers in the story- the Aegis Kai Doru are, canonically, major players of that Era. They seek after the hidden treasures of Constantinople and hunt after the witches who enter the city as they seek new mysteries to solve. The Ksirafai, which were mentioned in the previous Era, have lost most of their influence and have been reduced from a proud conspiracy with access to holy machinery and control over the Imperial Guards of the empire into a mere compact- but not for long. Building themselves around the new Janissary caste, they are able to regain much of their status and eventually get their former glory- even if they have to constantly check for demonic influence. With so many hints about dangerous Nightmares going out of control it is safe to assume that somehow, the God Machine was able to stop the Devouring from taking place, banishing the influence of Beasts and the Primordial Dream- and now they come en masses, and their Dark Mother may come with them- which means we need a group who deals with dreams and nightmares, that is someone who focus around Changelings and Beasts. With so many dead, the Ebony Fangs are surely around, hunting both ghosts and the Bound- and chasing that mysterious assassin (anyone knows who ti may be?). Perhaps a mummy focused group would also be appropriate, especially one focused around the Devourer- but the Faithful of Shulpae would also won't be out of place, especially considering the influence of the dread goddess. Also, we have a chance of explore Eastern Europe and its local groups- such as the Orthodox Strain of Cursed Blood who call upon the blood of dragons to fight demons- both Unchained and not.<br /> <br /> This is a time in which Heaven itself Fell to Hell- there are demons everywhere and dangers in every corner, but it won't stay like that forever. It would rebuild itself, stronger and better.<br /> <br /> And the Vigil would light the candles to guide it forward.<br /> <br /> any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T12:00:32-08:00","id":1031721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1031712#post1031712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, I did had a rough concept for them in that Era. If you want to discuss it, I think it would be better to do so at PMs or at the Vigilant Times thread, so we won't derail this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, right now, I am wondering if the Norse somehow have stories that speak of the Nibiru, who probably have been visiting their homelands way before the Vikings began their raids.<br /> <br /> And then I had this idea. What if the Nibiru were the inspiration for a particular group of spirits or goddesses of protection? What if they formed the basis of the Disir?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T04:22:47-08:00","id":1032583,"title":"","content":"Incomplete draft for Nibiru tie-in to TW&amp;TR and Acro's Fall of Fenris. <hr /><br /> <u><b>The Wolf and the Raven: Breakers of Chains</b></u><br /> <br /> For as long its people can remember, the Nibiru have visited the North. They bound many ancient spirits and elder gods, and worked to ensure that none could escape their prisons. Each of these horrors once preyed on humankind in ages past, and they would wreak untold havoc on the land should they somehow be unleashed.<br /> <br /> The First Hunters' sojourns do not go unnoticed. Many tales speak of these strange women who hail from the lands of the Byzantine Empire. Their <i>seidr</i> and ceremonies inspired both awe and fear, for it is said that they worked to prevent Ragnarok until the einherjar are ready to face it. Some stories even equate the Nine Daughters to the Disir, of whom the Valkyries are counted among. However they were portrayed, the Nibiru were given much respect in the Norselands, and it served them well in their Vigil.<br /> <br /> But while they hunted down dark gods so they may be bound or slain, they also fought them to release a mighty prisoner of theirs.<br /> <br /> The Nibiru know of the jotnar, and how they came to be in the mortal world. They recognized the threat they posed, and have long struggled to end it since the days of the Roman Empire. However, they never expected them to grow strong and cunning enough to bind a Firstborn, and the fiercest among their number no less. Now, Fenris-Ur lies locked away in their lands, and his power is slowly but surely being drained through the magic of his captors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T09:04:06-08:00","id":1037865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=930248#post930248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>-Collega Chironos</b> (Greece, freed slaves who use their knowledge of medicine to heal the sick and use beasts to make men into heroes)</div> </div> </div> </div>Too early to use Latin like that IMO. The &quot;slave&quot; angle was something I went with for &quot;Vigil for Rome&quot; because of the role of educated Greek slaves in the Roman Empire. I'm not sure how that angle plays in the Hellenistic Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:07:59-08:00","id":1038747,"title":"","content":"I was tinkering with a high medieval setting (12th &amp; 13th Centuries) - I'm thinking that the Sacred Order of the Knights of Saint George should be the dominant Conspiracy in Western Christendom (as well as the Crusader states). They exist as a faction of the Knights Templar. The distinctly English order is what's left after the fall of the Templars.<br /> <br /> So Conspiracy wise that's the Knights of Saint George in Western Christendom, Aegis Kai Doru in Eastern Christendom, the Ascending Ones throughout the Umma, and the Lucifuge scattered in the shadows wherever particular cursed houses and bloodlines might arise.<br /> <br /> I'm intentionally leaving this as a blank space in the history of Cheiron - my thinking is that the Cult of the Sign has gathered and been destroyed multiple times in history until others rediscover the Sign and the Cult is reborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T06:11:05-08:00","id":1038856,"title":"","content":"I don't know if anyone has said this yet, but i think that Sundered World Era is far enough back that Heroes are actually still uncorrupted. They might even be useful allies to Hunters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 01-27-2017, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T06:35:52-08:00","id":1038860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/923441-vigilant-times-take-2-open-invite?p=1038856#post1038856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if anyone has said this yet, but i think that Sundered World Era is far enough back that Heroes are actually still uncorrupted. They might even be useful allies to Hunters</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> covered that in his Sundered World Chronicles thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdo